BLE ADD COLUMN ... UNIQUE (confirmed silent no-op in SQLite, project memory feedback_sqlite_add_column_unique_silent_noop).\n\nDELIBERATE DEVIATION FROM THE LITERAL MANDATE KEY, evidence-backed: the WHERE payload != '{}' clause excludes alertStore.ts's verified_decision correlation-stub co-write (from_agent='alert-engine'). RAW-verified live: payload='{}' is used EXCLUSIVELY (zero other from_agent/signal_type combos) by this pattern, and it is a DESIGNED CONSTANT (the correlation stub links via alert_id, not payload content) — 51/202 live rows. That pattern ALREADY has a precise, narrower, alert_id-scoped dedup guard (FIX-AGENT-SIGNALS-ORPHAN-ALERT-ID, done-live-verified) built specifically because the payload carries zero differentiating content. Applying the coarser (minute+payload) key to it too would risk SILENTLY DROPPING a legitimate 2nd correlation stub whenever 2 genuinely-different real alerts (e.g. one taAlertScanJob TA alert + one bbAlertScanJob BB alert) fire for the same stock in the same minute — both are real, distinct alerts.id rows (different fingerprints), and each deserves its own agent_signals.alert_id-linked correlation row for the C-08 orphan-audit check. Verified this scenario is structurally possible (8 different mcp-server call sites co-write this exact from_agent/signal_type/payload tuple) even though it was NOT observed in the current live sample — the exclusion is a preventive correctness safeguard, not scope creep, and is fully documented (code comments in schema-news.ts + this note + decision journal STEP dev-mcp-server-S2).\n\nSTEP 3 PER-EMITTER ROOT-CAUSE (in-zone only, per boundary_rules): of the 5 emitters named in the mandate, ONLY freshness-sla-monitor is a genuine mcp-server-internal scheduler job — system-auditor/news-scout/bctc-analyst all post via the generic post_agent_signal MCP tool from cowork-agent sessions running OUTSIDE mcp-server's process (their own cron/spawn double-trigger root, if any, is out of dev-mcp-server's zone per boundary_rules — noted, not reached into). freshness-sla-monitor: code review (escalateToCommander() + the TASK-FFT-L4 coverage-map second pass, both in freshnessSlaMonitorJob.ts) confirms every postSignal() call embeds a live millisecond `timestamp: new Date().toISOString()` field in payload — present since the file's creation (git blame confirmed, predates the 2026-06-25 finding) — structurally CANNOT produce a byte-identical duplicate payload even under confirmed-live scheduler re-entrancy. Does not reproduce this defect class; does not share r2's root in a way that manifests here (r2 itself remains untouched, separate board row, still BACKLOG).\n\nalert-engine is NOT one cowork agent — RAW code review found it is the from_agent tag hardcoded in alertStore.ts's storeAlerts()/storeAlertsFromCommander() co-write, called from 8 different mcp-server scheduler call sites (taAlertScanJob, bbAlertScanJob, foreignFlowAlertJob, predictionMarketJob, intelligenceCycleJob, checkSscReports, pollNews, scanMarket). 7/8 already use a deterministic alerts.id (code+alertType+day or code+day bucket schemes), safe under scheduler re-entrancy via the existing alerts.fingerprint / id-collision INSERT OR IGNORE gates. scanMarket.ts (via domain/services/alertGenerator.ts's chooseAlertId() 'otherwise' fallback branch, used whenever a signal group is neither a single price-movement type nor a single news_mention type — e.g. report_new) used a random id() with NO fingerprint set at all — domain/services/alertDedup.ts's computeAlertFingerprint() has existed since Task 131 with ZERO production callers (confirmed via repo-wide grep) — i.e. dead/unwired code. This is the most plausible concrete root cause of the historical DPM 0.9s-apart genuine-duplicate agent_signals.verified_decision sample the task cites (ids 7269 & 7271): a re-entrant scanMarket() call (scheduler re-entrancy, RAW-confirmed still live via cron_job_runs) would mint 2 independent random alerts.id values with no fingerprint-based dedup at all. FIXED: new computeGenericAlertFingerprint(actionCode, signalTypes, message, detectedAt) in alertDedup.ts (deliberately a NARROW 1-minute bucket, unlike computeScanAlertFingerprint's 1-day bucket, so a genuinely-recurring one-time event on a LATER cycle is never suppressed — only truly-simultaneous re-executions collapse), wired into generateAlerts() (alertGenerator.ts) unconditionally on every Alert object — feeds the EXISTING alerts.fingerprint UNIQUE partial index already relied on by the other 7 call sites.\n\nSTEP 4 VERIFY-DON'T-CLAIM: traced every consumer of signal_type='verified_decision' AND from_agent='alert-engine'. It is a write-only correlation stub (payload always the literal '{}', linked via alert_id) — consumed ONLY by the C-08 orphaned-alerts audit check (checkOrphanAgentSignalsAlertId.ts). stockSignalsHandler.ts explicitly DROPS empty verified_decision rows from at least one display path, corroborating zero downstream consumer keys off this row's content. The REAL Telegram/MARKET dispatch path is driven directly from the alerts table by alert-commander (a cowork agent) — which has its OWN, SEPARATE verified_decision broadcast mechanism (from_agent='alert-commander' per its own docs/agents/alert-commander/init.md, fired AFTER it decides to send-or-suppress to MARKET — not what the PO's 24h dup-attribution query measured, since that query grouped by from_agent). CONFIRMED: no double-Telegram-alert risk from this duplicate class — held at P2, NOT escalated, per the mandate's own 'only escalate if genuinely confirmed' instruction.\n\nEvidence: new apps/mcp-server/src/__tests__/FIX-AGENT-SIGNALS-IDENTICAL-DUP-EMISSION.test.ts, 10/10 pass — AC-1..6 cover the data-layer backstop (byte-identical suppression, different-payload/different-stock non-suppression, NULL stock_code COALESCE handling, the payload='{}' exclusion proven safe via direct raw-SQL insert mirroring alertStore.ts's own shape, and a legacy-DB-without-the-index no-o